## Pattern C: Reverse number pattern

Output:

```
12345
1234
123
12
1
```

Code:

```

using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        for (int i = 5; i >= 1; i--)
        {
            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++)
            {
                Console.Write(j);
            }

            Console.WriteLine();
        }

        Console.ReadLine();
    }
}

```

## Pattern D: Continuous number triangle

Output:

```
1
23
456
78910
```

Code:

```

using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        int num = 1;

        for (int i = 1; i <= 4; i++)
        {
            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++)
            {
                Console.Write(num);
                num++;
            }

            Console.WriteLine();
        }

        Console.ReadLine();
    }
}

```

## The nested-loop trick to remember

| Code                  | Meaning                                     |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| `i`                   | Controls the row                            |
| `j`                   | Controls how many numbers print in each row |
| `Console.Write()`     | Prints on the same line                     |
| `Console.WriteLine()` | Moves to the next line                      |
| `j <= i`              | Prints more numbers in each successive row  |

Exam tip: If the pattern changes row by row, think of a nested `for` loop.

